---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="Who Runs Spokdom"
	description={`Meet the person behind ${SITE_TITLE} and the editorial rules every review follows.`}
	pubDate={new Date('August 25 2026')}
>
	<h2>Hi, I'm Sungbin</h2>
	<p>
		I build and run <strong>{SITE_TITLE}</strong> on my own. I'm not an analyst at a research
		firm — I'm a solo builder based in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam, who ships web projects and
		pays for a lot of software out of my own pocket.
	</p>

	<p>
		That's exactly why this site exists. Every "best tools" list I found was either an
		affiliate dump or a feature table copied from the vendor's own marketing page. What I
		actually wanted to know was simpler: <em
			>does this thing hold up after a week of real use, and what breaks when it doesn't?</em
		>
	</p>

	<h2>How reviews here work</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Hands-on first.</strong> When I've used a tool myself, I say so. When a piece
			is built from documentation, pricing pages, and other users' reports, I say that too —
			I never dress up research as personal experience.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Downsides go up top.</strong> If a tool is wrong for you, you should know
			within the first screen, not after 2,000 words.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Pricing is dated.</strong> SaaS pricing changes constantly, so every price
			states when it was checked.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Corrections are fast.</strong> Tell me something is wrong and I verify it and
			fix the article — vendors included.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>How this site makes money</h2>
	<p>
		Some links are affiliate links. If you sign up through one, I may earn a commission at no
		extra cost to you. <strong>It never changes a verdict.</strong> No vendor gets to review,
		approve, or influence a piece before it goes live. Details on advertising and cookies are
		in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>
	<p>
		Corrections, tools you want covered, and partnership questions are all welcome.<br />
		📧 <a href="mailto:yangsungbin77@gmail.com">yangsungbin77@gmail.com</a>
	</p>
	<p>
		I usually reply within 2–3 days. The same address is on the <a href="/contact">contact</a>
		page.
	</p>
</Layout>
